        "original_id": "fbd359d7-001a-5648-9009-cbb6f49f1e3a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Betzy Kjelsberg, Ole Gabriel Rasch\n- Places: Svelvik, Vestfold, Botne, Hole, Norway, Buskerud, Telemark\n- Organizations: Liberal Party, Team Sky, UCI ProTeam\n- Roles: politician, factory inspector, feminist, road bicycle racer, directeur sportif\n\nFacts:\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was born as Betzy Aleksandra Børresen on 1 November 1866 in Svelvik, Vestfold, Norway.\n- Vestfold is a county in Norway that borders Buskerud and Telemark.\n- Botne was a municipality in Vestfold county, Norway.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was a Norwegian politician for the Liberal Party, the first female board member of the party, Norway's first female factory inspector from 1910 to 1936, and a member of the feminist movement.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg died on 3 October 1950.\n- Ole Gabriel Rasch was born on 8 April 1976 in Hole, Norway.\n- Ole Gabriel Rasch is a Norwegian former road bicycle racer who works as a directeur sportif for UCI ProTeam Team Sky.",
